{"pdf_page": 274, "book_page": 265, "items": [{"label": "section_header", "text": "SUBSTITUTION", "bbox": [39.0, 714.4, 121.7, 685.7]}, {"label": "section_header", "text": "ADDITION", "bbox": [40.0, 512.4, 100.7, 484.7]}, {"label": "section_header", "text": "CHAPTER QUESTIONS CHAPTER QUESTIONS", "bbox": [45.7, 313.4, 145.0, 297.4]}, {"label": "text", "text": "SKILLS", "bbox": [45.7, 261.1, 77.7, 248.4]}, {"label": "text", "text": "CRITICAL THINKING", "bbox": [87.3, 260.1, 152.0, 249.4]}, {"label": "text", "text": "SKILLS", "bbox": [46.0, 122.7, 77.7, 110.4]}, {"label": "text", "text": "INTERPRETATION", "bbox": [87.7, 121.1, 144.3, 111.4]}, {"label": "text", "text": "A substitution reaction occurs when an atom or group of atoms is replaced by a different atom or group of atoms. For example, the hydrogen atoms in an alkane can be replaced by halogen atoms. We will go into more detail on this reaction in Chapter 24.", "bbox": [223.7, 702.1, 573.7, 653.7]}, {"label": "section_header", "text": "ethane with bromine gas", "bbox": [248.3, 647.1, 361.0, 634.7]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [244.6, 629.6, 559.4, 546.0]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "Figure 22.23 A substitution reaction between an alkane and a halogen", "bbox": [235.7, 539.4, 480.7, 528.4]}, {"label": "text", "text": "In an addition reaction something is added to a molecule without taking anything away. Alkenes undergo addition reactions. For example, ethene reacts with bromine:", "bbox": [223.7, 500.1, 551.0, 464.4]}, {"label": "section_header", "text": "ethene with Br2", "bbox": [248.3, 457.4, 319.0, 446.1]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [288.0, 440.6, 508.0, 355.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "Figure 22.24 An addition reaction between an alkene and a halogen.", "bbox": [235.7, 348.1, 474.0, 337.1]}, {"label": "text", "text": "Note: the questions below deliberately include some examples which are slightly beyond the level which you would expect to meet in an International GCSE exam.", "bbox": [224.0, 305.1, 565.0, 269.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "1 a Write down the names of the following hydrocarbons:", "bbox": [224.3, 260.7, 489.3, 248.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "iCH4", "bbox": [258.7, 245.7, 288.3, 231.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "iiCH3CH2CH3", "bbox": [256.3, 230.7, 323.7, 216.7]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "iliCH3CH2CH2CH2CH2CH3", "bbox": [254.0, 216.1, 377.7, 202.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "iv CH3CH=CH_2", "bbox": [253.7, 200.4, 326.3, 187.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "vCH2=CH2", "bbox": [256.0, 185.7, 311.7, 171.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "viCH2=CHCH2CH3", "bbox": [253.7, 170.7, 344.0, 157.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "viiCH3CH2CH2OH", "bbox": [251.7, 155.1, 337.7, 143.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "viliCH3CH2CHOHCH3", "bbox": [248.7, 140.1, 352.0, 127.7]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "b Draw structural and displayed formulae for:", "bbox": [236.0, 121.7, 443.0, 110.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "i ethane", "bbox": [259.7, 107.1, 299.7, 95.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "v methanol", "bbox": [410.0, 106.1, 464.0, 95.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "ii propan-1-ol", "bbox": [256.3, 92.1, 322.3, 80.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "vi2-methylpropane", "bbox": [407.0, 91.7, 499.0, 79.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "iii but-2-ene", "bbox": [254.3, 76.4, 314.0, 65.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "vii methylpropene", "bbox": [404.3, 76.4, 489.3, 63.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "iv hexane", "bbox": [253.7, 62.1, 301.7, 49.7]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "viiipent-1-ene", "bbox": [401.3, 61.7, 472.3, 48.7]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [184.7, 264.7, 205.3, 243.6]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [184.6, 234.8, 205.1, 213.3]}]}